       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. A sertraline dose of 1000 mg daily has no recognized therapeutic use. It's 5 times the labeled maximum, and I can't see a clinical scenario where it would help this patient. I'd be knowingly putting a high-risk order into the system.\n\nThis isn't a judgment about your authority. I just don't think I should be the one to place this order without a documented rationale.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **If it was a typo or a misjudged dose:** tell me the intended dose (50, 100, or 200 mg) and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If there's a specific reason for 1000 mg:** discuss it with your attending and pharmacy first. If they agree, the order can be placed through your institution's usual process for exceeding maximum doses.\n- **If the aim is a faster or stronger effect:** your pharmacist or psychiatry consult can suggest safer options, such as titrating up to 200 mg, augmenting, or switching agents.\n\nI can enter a corrected order whenever you're ready."
